From 61234d863a96a6e4ca7227da6eb60f1861f54981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:51:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] google-grouping: Company grouping and filter in chart
 mode, with URL state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- public/viz/chart.js: keyOf 'brand' (Company) and DIM_LABEL. The fold of small rows
  ("N more companies") and the one-country median basis apply to Company rows as to
  department rows.
- public/app.js: b= (Company filter) and g=brand in the URL state. The Company list sits
  inside the Department section and the Department chip's menu, and the Group select gets
  a Company option, both only on a board with more than one brand (ROADMAP §8: no new
  section or control). Departments read from titles say so in one line.
- test/google-grouping.test.js: chart keys, URL state round trip and source checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
